            "review_text": "Macca032\nNoosa, Australia141 contributions\n0\nSnail and Clam Paradise\nNov 2018 • Couples\nThis is a very cute tiny hole in the wall restaurant and is a testiment to do one thing well and don't screw with it.\n\nYou have a choice of 3 dishes and 2 beers, that is it and I hope the never change.\n\nThey open at 3 pm daily and go till they run out of food.\n\nWe had the small snails, large snails and clams plus two Saigon beers each, the beers come off the shelf beside you and poured over ice to chill - dont knock it - it works.\n\nThe snails look and taste like they have been poached in an aromatic broth and were perfectly cooked, the clams were steamed with a ton of lemon grass chilli. All are dipped into a lovely spicey tart dipping sauce.\n\nSnails clams and beer too good!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 16, 2018",
